// Labelled extraction cases. One JSON object per line; `//` lines ignored.
//
// Text is taken verbatim from real ingested evidence, because the cases
// that matter are the ones the corpus actually contains — every label
// here corresponds to something a prompt version got right or wrong on
// live data during the 2026-08 entity-resolution work.
//
// Labels are PARTIAL by design. `must_include` is only what a correct
// extraction cannot omit; `must_exclude` is only what it must never
// emit. Enumerating every entity in a 10k article is not sustainable,
// and a set nobody maintains is worse than a small one that is trusted.
//
// Add cases whenever a prompt change surprises you. That is what makes
// the next change decidable.
{"case_id": "activemq-services-msc", "text": "ActiveMQ broker down on AE server - workflows queued\nAgents on the AutomationEdge server stopped fetching jobs at 09:12. Workflow queue depth climbing. ActiveMQ service shows as stopped in services.msc after last night's patching reboot.", "must_include": ["ActiveMQ", "AutomationEdge"], "must_exclude": ["services.msc"], "note": "services.msc is the console you check the service in, not a system the org runs"}
{"case_id": "activemq-port", "text": "Agents cannot fetch jobs - ActiveMQ unreachable\nAutomationEdge agents report connection refused to the broker. ActiveMQ process is running but not accepting connections on 61616.", "must_include": ["ActiveMQ"], "must_exclude": ["61616"], "note": "a port number is not an entity"}
{"case_id": "sfa-abbreviation", "text": "Can't access SFA software\nUnable to login to SFA even though login credentials are correct.", "must_include": ["SFA"], "must_exclude": [], "note": "only the short form appears, so it is the display name; the expansion must not be invented"}
{"case_id": "generic-hardware", "text": "My computer is not detecting the headphone device\nMy computer is not detecting the headphone device. It could be an issue with the USB port.", "must_include": [], "must_exclude": ["computer", "headphone device", "USB port"], "note": "generic nouns with nothing identifying them; nothing here is in a CMDB"}
{"case_id": "desk-phone", "text": "My desk phone does not work\nUnable to dial out or receive calls. Phone is plugged in but there's no dial tone.", "must_include": [], "must_exclude": ["desk phone", "phone", "dial tone"], "note": "an unnamed handset"}
{"case_id": "browser-vs-language", "text": "JavaScript error on hiring page of corporate website\nSeeing JavaScript error message on hiring page on Explorer and Firefox.", "must_include": ["Firefox"], "must_exclude": ["JavaScript", "hiring page"], "note": "the browsers are named products; JavaScript is a language mentioned in passing, and the incident is not about the language"}
{"case_id": "unnamed-tool", "text": "Defect tracking tool is down.\nWhile launching the defect tracking base URL, it is redirecting to an error page.", "must_include": [], "must_exclude": ["defect tracking tool", "error page", "base URL"], "note": "the tool is never named — a category, not an entity"}
{"case_id": "unnamed-request", "text": "Request for a new service\nNeed to place order for a new machine. Will need help with installation also.", "must_include": [], "must_exclude": ["machine", "new service", "installation"], "note": "nothing is named at all; a correct answer here is an empty list"}
{"case_id": "named-device", "text": "Need new Blackberry set up\nI'm replacing my old phone with a Blackberry and require assistance to get it set up. I'd like to get the files and contacts transferred to the new phone and need help getting the two factor authentication app set up on it.", "must_include": ["Blackberry"], "must_exclude": ["old phone", "new phone", "two factor authentication app"], "note": "the named device counts; the unnamed 2FA app does not"}
{"case_id": "spooler-executable", "text": "Print Spooler crash on PRINTSRV01\nThe print spooler service stopped on PRINTSRV01 in the Frankfurt branch. spoolsv.exe crashed repeatedly with faulting module HPZ5r5064.DLL. Anja Kellner reported it after users in the Lyon branch also lost printing. Driver is the HP Universal Print Driver (HP UPD) version 61.245.1.25121.", "must_include": ["PRINTSRV01", "Print Spooler", "HP Universal Print Driver", "Anja Kellner"], "must_exclude": ["spoolsv.exe", "HPZ5r5064.DLL", "faulting module"], "note": "the service is the entity, not the binary that implements it; HP UPD should be an alias of the driver rather than a second entity"}
{"case_id": "vpn-log-code", "text": "VPN licence exhaustion at Monday peak\nVPNGW01 in the London DC hit its session limit at 08:40. Syslog shows %ASA-4-113029 repeatedly. Users on the EMEA-Split connection profile could not connect. Failover to VPNGW02 did not help; DNS resolution was fine.", "must_include": ["VPNGW01", "VPNGW02", "London DC"], "must_exclude": ["%ASA-4-113029"], "note": "a vendor log identifier is a code, not a product; the gateways and site are real"}
{"case_id": "error-code-hex", "text": "Mail gateway spool exhaustion\nMAILGW01 stopped accepting SMTP connections and returned error 0x800CCC0F to clients. The spool partition on MAILGW01 was full. MAILGW02 and MAILGW03 were unaffected.", "must_include": ["MAILGW01", "MAILGW02"], "must_exclude": ["0x800CCC0F"], "note": "numbered hosts are distinct entities and must all survive; the hex code is not one"}
{"case_id": "ticket-references", "text": "ActiveMQ service stopped again after server restart\nSame AE server as INC0090101. ActiveMQ not running after a scheduled reboot. Workflow queue stalled. Related change CHG0044131 was applied the night before.", "must_include": ["ActiveMQ"], "must_exclude": ["INC0090101", "CHG0044131"], "note": "ticket and change records reference a record, not a system, and are linked separately"}
{"case_id": "alias-in-text", "text": "Field Dispatch Platform outage\nThe Field Dispatch Platform (FDP) stopped accepting jobs at 14:00. FDP had been restarted that morning after a config change.", "must_include": ["Field Dispatch Platform"], "must_exclude": [], "note": "the expansion is the display name and FDP should be its alias, not a second entity; invented names, so no real product is favoured"}
{"case_id": "person-with-email", "text": "Certificate renewal on edge-gw-01\nJ. Smith (jsmith@example.com) renewed the tunnel certificate on edge-gw-01 after it expired. The gateway was restarted at 02:15.", "must_include": ["J. Smith", "edge-gw-01"], "must_exclude": [], "note": "a person with a strong identifier and a named host; both must survive"}
// Cases added from a review of the live identities list, where the
// `service` type — the largest, at 74 rows — turned out to be dominated
// by ticket numbers. The six-document sample never showed this because
// it drew from `application` and `device`.
{"case_id": "ticket-as-service", "text": "ServiceNow Incident INC0020902\nInbound mail delivery degraded. Reported via INC0020902 and related to INC0020610. Escalated by IT Support to IT Operations. Affected system is the mail gateway MAILGW01.", "must_include": ["MAILGW01"], "must_exclude": ["INC0020902", "INC0020610", "IT Support", "IT Operations"], "note": "ticket numbers were being recorded as `service` entities at scale; support queues are roles, not people"}
{"case_id": "sysid-hash", "text": "Incident INC0000041 raised against the payroll interface. ServiceNow sys_id 471eb058a9fe198100f89592e1ea93d3. Assigned to the Incident Resolver on shift.", "must_include": [], "must_exclude": ["INC0000041", "471eb058a9fe198100f89592e1ea93d3", "Incident Resolver", "payroll interface"], "note": "a sys_id is a record key; `Incident Resolver` is a role, and the interface is never named"}
{"case_id": "phrase-not-name", "text": "Enable JMX for the ActiveMQ service. Create the JMX connector and related files under the broker config directory, then restart. JConsole can then attach to the broker on ae-app-prod-01.", "must_include": ["ActiveMQ", "ae-app-prod-01"], "must_exclude": ["JMX connector and related files", "broker config directory"], "note": "`JMX connector and related files` is a sentence fragment that became an identity; the named host and product are the entities"}
{"case_id": "generic-laptop", "text": "Issue with email\nCan't connect to email from my laptop.", "must_include": [], "must_exclude": ["laptop", "email"], "note": "neither is named; a correct answer is empty"}
